{
  "rule_2e": "Phase 2e rule (fixed before this run). Matched positive controls whose labels come from CBM-B, an evaluator trained on Derm7pt expert labels and independent of the CBM-A pseudo-labels that condition the generator. For each concept (pigment network, vascular structures, pigmentation, regression structures): the low group is the bottom quartile and the high group the top quartile of the CBM-B output on the training split (if the top-quartile threshold is below 0.5, the high group is CBM-B output >= 0.5); 1:1 greedy nearest-neighbour matching without replacement on the other six standardised CBM-B outputs, Euclidean caliper 0.5 (1.0 if the training split has fewer than 100 pairs), exact on the melanoma label, within each split, random order with seed 3029 plus the concept index. A concept with fewer than 50 training pairs is not testable and its controls count as not passed. Four controls per concept: ResNet-50 seeds 1, 2, 3 and ViT-B/16 seed 1, with the Phase 2 training recipe. A control passes if its target knob has the largest effect, positive and significant (two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test on per-trajectory slopes, BH-corrected p < 0.05, median slope > 0), in at least 3 of 4 bases. GO for a concept if at least 3 of its 4 controls pass. The paper keeps the claim that the audit is validated only for concepts that are GO. Earlier verdicts are not changed.",
